new ConcurrentHashMap<>() -> table is null, sizeCtl 0
after  1 puts -> capacity 16, sizeCtl (next resize at) 12
after 12 puts -> capacity 32, sizeCtl (next resize at) 24
after 13 puts -> capacity 32, sizeCtl (next resize at) 24

Same shape as HashMap — an array of bins — but each bin is locked separately,
empty bins are filled with a CAS (no lock), and resizing is shared between threads.
